 "release_rule_decided": {
  "rule": "release the drogue at E2 AND [measured Pc >= 3.0 bar abs OR the >= 0.8 bar rise held continuously until E2 + 0.10 s]",
  "E2": "relative light confirmation: Pc rise >= 0.8 bar above the pre-lift baseline, held 10 ms (Combustion ignition_detect_v2p4: E2 14.0-15.5 ms after main ignition)",
  "Pc_abs_floor_Pa": 300000.0,
  "rise_Pa": 80000.0,
  "rise_hold_s": 0.01,
  "persistence_timeout_s": 0.1,
  "worst_case_hold_after_E2_s": 0.1,
  "decided": "LEAD 2026-10-13: GNC proposal (b) with the persistence check; a fixed absolute floor alone (proposal (a)) cannot separate lit from unlit at the +/-0.6 bar residual",
  "evidence": "m2_release_rule v1.2 (release_rule.json): release held after the light 0 / 100 / 200 / 400 ms -> pooled A1_none + A1J_pc lost/gained -1/+2, -4/+4, -11/+5 (p 0.21), -21/+6 (p 0.0059); the worst-case hold of this rule (0.10 s) is the P-neutral 100 ms bracket",
  "sim6_status": "amendment R implements 'E2 AND Pc >= 3.0 bar abs' (rel_mode 1; rel_F = map thrust at 3.0 bar abs, run6 DERIVED 37.2 N; rel_dt = E2 after the 6-DOF light). Amendment S implements the persistence branch: rel_to 0.10 s, rise evaluated as the Pc-equivalent thrust >= rel_Frise = map thrust at baseline + 0.8 bar = 2.113 bar abs (ISA 1.013 bar ASSUMED + torch 0.3 bar B-PC-1 target, upper) = 22.9 N; one step below it after E2 loses the branch. m2_bitcheck_v28 v1.5 part S: with the v2.8 thrust ramp the branch never acts (S1: 1000 runs, 0 persistence releases, every stored rel1 value reproduced); with a plateau below 3.0 bar it releases at E2 + 0.10 s (S2); a plateau above 3.0 bar releases on Pc (S3); a plateau below the rise threshold loses the branch (S4). Flown with the plateau in m2_start_transient v1 (RG-01 start-transient re-fly)",
  "flown_in_rev1": "rel_mode 0 (v2.8 model: truth F > 0.5 floor) in every rev1 base except the m2_release_rule arms (rel_mode 1, rel_to 0), the m2_start_transient arms (rel_mode 1, rel_to 0.10 except arm L400_nto) and the m2_purge_cost arms (rel_mode 1, rel_to 0.10)",
  "fc_implementation": {
   "tag": "DESIGN (GNC mapping of the LEAD rule onto the Electronics v2.9 telemetry; firmware v2.9 SIL only, not flown in hardware)",
   "frame": "TLM_FAST CAN 0x100 ECU->FC, 500 Hz, len 8: d0 seq; d1 = state in b0-b3 (EVERY FC decoder masks d1 & 0x0F; the unmasked byte is no longer the state) + flags b4 E2 of this start, b5 rise now (firmware v2.9: filtered AND raw >= P0 + 0.8 bar), b6 rise held since E2 (cleared at the first tick without it, stays clear for the start), b7 rise held to E2 + kDrogueRiseHold_s 0.10 s (latched); d2-d3 Pc u16 kPa abs (0xFFFF = invalid, RG-15); d4-d5 pintle lift; d6-d7 fault bits incl. PC_SENSOR. LEAD 2026-10-13 (CHANGELOG, after the Combustion drogue-hold check): the hold (b6/b7) is evaluated on the FILTERED channel only, E2 keeps filtered AND raw; to be implemented when Electronics resumes (firmware v2.9 still uses filtered AND raw for the hold)",
   "predicate": "while the drogue is attached in the A relight, on each new TLM_FAST frame (sequence advanced): RELEASE iff b4 AND [(d2-d3 != 0xFFFF AND d2-d3 >= 300 kPa abs) OR b7]; b5 and b6 are logged, not used; the decision is latched (one release command, never re-attached)",
   "e2_source": "b4 is set in the frame of the RUN entry; the E2 time is EVENT 0x120 STATE (RUN entry) t_ms",
   "sil_evidence": "Electronics SIL A1 relight (firmware v2.9, N 273 lit): rise held to E2 + 0.10 s in 273/273; E2 -> Pc 3.0 bar abs p50/p95/max 3/34/43 ms; E2 16-18 ms after the light (LEAD 2026-10-13: accepted); the SIL plant has no fuel-starved plateau",
   "sim6_equivalence": "sim6 rel_mode 1 + rel_to 0.10: E2 at the 6-DOF light (rel_dt 0), i.e. 16-18 ms EARLIER than the firmware; release bracket: +100 ms pooled -4/+4, +200 ms -11/+5 (p 0.21), +400 ms -21/+6 (p 0.0059) -> the 16-18 ms offset is inside the P-neutral bracket. Rise in sim6 = truth Pc-equivalent thrust >= rel_Frise (P0 = 1.313 bar abs ASSUMED); in firmware v2.9 the hold uses filtered AND raw over the measured P0, so roughness or a dip clears b6/b7 and the release falls back on the 3.0 bar branch (the LEAD filtered-only decision removes the raw-channel path); that direction is bounded by arm L400_nto (branch off; pooled -13/+6 p 0.167 vs the decided rule without plateau; branch on vs off -10/+12 p 0.832). Combustion drogue_hold_check_v2p4 (70820e0038be39a7, SIM quasi-steady, 288 lit corners): rise >= 0.8 bar held from E2 to E2 + 0.10 s on every lit corner, min margin 0.74 bar (0.48 bar with the torch +0.3 bar in the baseline only); no unlit case reaches 0.8 bar (max 0.51); worst corner (fuel-starved A1 relight) Pc 2.60-2.62 bar abs, between the flown plateau arms L (2.4 bar) and M (2.9 bar), neither of which loses; roughness tolerance 0.48 bar zero-to-peak, unmeasured until IGN-1/T1",
   "open_item": "Pc channel invalid inside [E2, release] (window <= 43 ms in SIL, up to 0.10 s on a plateau): neither branch can complete and the drogue stays attached while the engine runs; the decided rule does not define this case and sim6 has no Pc-invalid model in the release logic -> fault arm required (RG-15 extension); no value is proposed here",
   "sources": {
    "electronics_json": "/home/claude/work/shared-fallback/engine/interfaces/electronics.json (sha256/16 da067408c1594814)",
    "lead": "interfaces/CHANGELOG.md 2026-10-13 lead decisions on the release rule, on the Electronics handback ((4) E2 latency accepted, (6) d1 mask) and on the filtered-only hold bit",
    "combustion_drogue_hold": "/home/claude/work/combustion/data/v2/v2p4/drogue_hold_check_v2p4.json (sha256/16 70820e0038be39a7, read-only)"
   }
  }
 },
